{% comment %}
  "Priced with honesty" — a material comparison against typical UK retail.

  No competitor is named in the table. The claims sit at the level of what UK
  retailers in this band publish on their own product pages, and the retailers we
  read are credited in the footnote as sources. Evidence, exact wording rules, and
  the claims we are NOT entitled to make: docs/price-comparison-evidence.md.
  Re-verify before every release.

  Brook sits inside the high-street price band, so it carries a price row per size
  and the line is "same money, better mirror". Solenne at £749 is dearer than the
  two full-length pieces we could evidence (£425, £569), so it carries NO price row.
  We do not show a flattering number while hiding an unflattering one.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign show_comparison = false
  assign our_glass = ''
  assign their_bands = ''

  case product.handle
    when 'brook-champagne-gold-wall-mirror', 'brook-matte-black-wall-mirror'
      assign show_comparison = true
      assign our_glass = '4 mm, copper-free and lead-free'
      comment
        One band per size variant, in variant order. A single band would quote the
        small-mirror band beside the large mirror's price. Sources in the evidence file:
        73x52 -> La Redoute £120.99, G&G £129, M&S £139, Oliver Bonas £160, John Lewis £250
        90x65 -> Oliver Bonas £195, Atkin & Thyme £219, John Lewis £250, Cox & Cox £425
      endcomment
      assign their_bands = '£130 to £250|£195 to £425'
    when 'solenne-champagne-gold-full-length-mirror'
      assign show_comparison = true
      assign our_glass = '5 mm, copper-free and lead-free'
  endcase

  assign checked_on = '10 July 2026'
-%}

{%- if show_comparison -%}
<section class="honesty" aria-labelledby="honesty-title">
  <div class="container honesty-inner">

    <div class="honesty-head">
      <span class="honesty-eyebrow">Priced with honesty</span>
      <h2 class="honesty-title" id="honesty-title">The difference is in the frame</h2>
      <p class="honesty-lede">
        Two asymmetrical mirrors can look identical in a photograph and be made of
        completely different things. So we read what UK shops say their frames are
        actually made of.
      </p>
    </div>

    <table class="honesty-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col"><span class="honesty-vh">Comparison</span></th>
          <th scope="col" class="honesty-us">MUNLER</th>
          <th scope="col">Typical UK retail</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Frame</th>
          <td class="honesty-us">304 stainless steel</td>
          <td>Iron, wood or MDF</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Glass</th>
          <td class="honesty-us">{{ our_glass }}</td>
          <td>Not stated</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Warranty</th>
          <td class="honesty-us">5 years</td>
          <td>Not stated</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">UK delivery</th>
          <td class="honesty-us">Free, insured, tracked</td>
          <td>Often charged</td>
        </tr>
        {%- if their_bands != blank -%}
          {%- assign band_list = their_bands | split: '|' -%}
          {%- assign size_idx = 0 -%}
          {%- for variant in product.variants -%}
            {%- assign vt = variant.title | downcase -%}
            {%- unless vt == 'default title' -%}
              {%- assign band = band_list[size_idx] -%}
              {%- if band -%}
                {%- assign size_label = variant.title | split: ' - ' | first -%}
                <tr class="honesty-row--price">
                  <th scope="row">{{ size_label }}</th>
                  <td class="honesty-us"><span class="honesty-price">{{ variant.price | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span></td>
                  <td><span class="honesty-price honesty-price--them">{{ band }}</span></td>
                </tr>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- assign size_idx = size_idx | plus: 1 -%}
            {%- endunless -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      </tbody>
    </table>

    {%- if their_bands != blank -%}
    <p class="honesty-kicker">Same money. Better mirror.</p>
    {%- else -%}
    <p class="honesty-kicker">Built to outlast the room it hangs in.</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    <p class="honesty-foot">
      Frame materials as published by Dunelm, John Lewis, Oliver Bonas, La Redoute,
      Cox &amp; Cox and Atkin &amp; Thyme on their own product pages, for asymmetrical wall
      mirrors between £120 and £400, checked on {{ checked_on }}. Iron and wood are honest
      materials. They are simply not the same materials.
    </p>

  </div>
</section>
{%- endif -%}
